# What never needs to reach the build context.
#
# Two reasons to care beyond speed. A context that carries node_modules ships one
# platform's native builds into a multi-platform build, and `npm ci` in the image
# would then be layered on top of them. And a context that carries .next or out
# means a stale local build can be copied into an image that looks freshly built.

node_modules
.next
out

# Local tooling and history. None of it is input to the build.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.specify
specs
docs
tests
*.log

# The one that would defeat the whole point of this feature: a config.json a
# maintainer wrote for their own machine, baked into a published image. The image
# gets config.example.json, copied explicitly by the Dockerfile.
config.json

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs and metadata that change nothing about the output.
README.md
LICENSE
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
